  "name": "@aleph-alpha/lib-mcp",
  "readme": "# @aleph-alpha/lib-mcp\n\nMCP (Model Context Protocol) Server for UI Library and ChatKit component discovery tools.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis package provides an MCP server that enables AI assistants (like Claude and Cursor) to discover and understand components from:\n\n- [`@aleph-alpha/ui-library`](../ui-library) \u2014 `Ui*` components\n- [`@aleph-alpha/chat-kit`](../chat-kit) \u2014 `Ck*` components\n\nIt offers tools to list available components and retrieve detailed documentation including props, examples, and usage guidance.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall `@aleph-alpha/lib-mcp` together with the component packages whose docs you want to query. UI Library is required; ChatKit is optional and only needed if you want `Ck*` component docs.\n\n```bash\n# UI Library only\npnpm add @aleph-alpha/lib-mcp @aleph-alpha/ui-library\n\n# UI Library + ChatKit\npnpm add @aleph-alpha/lib-mcp @aleph-alpha/ui-library @aleph-alpha/chat-kit\n```\n\n> ChatKit docs require `@aleph-alpha/chat-kit` to publish its `src/` directory (component `types.ts` and `*.stories.ts` files). If `get_chat_kit_docs` returns \"Could not find chat-kit source directory\", upgrade `@aleph-alpha/chat-kit` to a version that includes `src/` in its published files.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Configure MCP Server\n\nRun the install command to configure your IDE:\n\n```bash\n# For Claude Code\nnpx @aleph-alpha/lib-mcp mcp-install\n\n# For both Claude Code and Cursor\nnpx @aleph-alpha/lib-mcp mcp-install --cursor\n\n# For VS Code\nnpx @aleph-alpha/lib-mcp mcp-install --vscode\n```\n\nAfter installation, restart your IDE to activate the MCP tools.\n\n### Available MCP Tools\n\nOnce configured, the following tools are available to your AI assistant:\n\n#### UI Library tools\n\n##### `list_components`\n\nLists all available UI Library components. Supports optional filtering by name, category, or description.\n\n```\nlist_components\nlist_components --filter=\"button\"\nlist_components --filter=\"form\"\n```\n\n##### `get_component_docs`\n\nRetrieves full documentation for a specific UI Library component including:\n\n- Component description\n- Props with types, defaults, and descriptions\n- Sub-components (if applicable)\n- Usage guidance\n- Code examples\n\n```\nget_component_docs UiButton\nget_component_docs Button  # \"Ui\" prefix is optional\n```\n\n#### ChatKit tools\n\nAvailable when `@aleph-alpha/chat-kit` is installed alongside this package.\n\n##### `list_chat_kit_components`\n\nLists all available ChatKit (`Ck*`) components. Supports optional filtering by name, category, or description.\n\n```\nlist_chat_kit_components\nlist_chat_kit_components --filter=\"history\"\nlist_chat_kit_components --filter=\"message\"\n```\n\n##### `get_chat_kit_docs`\n\nRetrieves full documentation for a specific ChatKit component, with the same shape as `get_component_docs`:\n\n- Component description\n- Props with types, defaults, and descriptions\n- Sub-components (if applicable)\n- Usage guidance\n- Code examples\n\n```\nget_chat_kit_docs CkHistory\nget_chat_kit_docs History  # \"Ck\" prefix is optional\n```\n\n#### Setup tool\n\n##### `get_setup_guide`\n\nReturns the setup and installation guide for integrating the UI library into a project (UnoCSS config, Vite config, required dependencies, and MCP setup instructions).\n\n```\nget_setup_guide\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Building\n\n```bash\npnpm build\n```\n\n### Generating Component Metadata\n\nRegenerates `components-meta.json` (UI Library) and `chat-kit-components-meta.json` (ChatKit) by scanning each package's source files.\n\n```bash\npnpm generate:component-meta\n```\n\n### Testing\n\n```bash\npnpm test\n```\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe MCP server reads component metadata from each package's source layout:\n\n1. **`types.ts`**: Extracts props, their types, descriptions, and component-level JSDoc tags (`@category`, `@useCases`, `@keywords`, `@related`)\n2. **`*.stories.ts`**: Extracts code examples and usage guidance from Storybook stories\n3. **`index.ts`**: Detects sub-component exports for the documented component\n4. **`components-meta.json` / `chat-kit-components-meta.json`**: Pre-generated metadata for faster lookups\n\nUI Library components are read from `@aleph-alpha/ui-library/src/**`, and ChatKit components from `@aleph-alpha/chat-kit/src/components/**`. Both packages must publish their `src/` directory for docs to resolve when consumed from `node_modules`.\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n| Command       | Description                                                             |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mcp-install` | Configure MCP server for IDE (`--cursor`, `--vscode` to add extra IDEs) |\n| `serve`       | Start the MCP server (used internally by IDE)                           |\n| `--help`      | Show help message                                                       |\n\n## License\n\nApache-2.0\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
